      "content": "the rose of Jericho, a small annual cruciferous plant (Anastatica hierochuntina), the dried fronds of which unfold under the influence of moisture (OED s.v. rose of Jericho) | Rose of Jericho, a small annual cruciferous plant (Anastatica hierochuntina), native to the arid deserts of South-west Asia and North-east Africa, the dried fronds of which unfold under the influence of moisture (OED s.v. Mary 1c, rose of Jericho) | probably St. Mary's herb (costmary), used in medicine and to flavour ale (OED s.v. herb 7b) rather than St. Mary's flower, Rose of Jericho (OED s.v. Mary 1c)"
    }
